# Owned by the service account, mode 400. The calling uid cannot read this.
#
# This file is sourced by a shell wrapper, so any value holding a space or a brace has to be
# single-quoted. DRIVE_LIBRARIES below is the one that does.
#
# The app-specific password is generated at account.apple.com under Sign-In
# and Security → App-Specific Passwords, and is revocable there without
# touching anything else. Do not put the primary Apple password here.
#
# ICLOUD_APPLE_ID       The account this server speaks for.
# ICLOUD_APP_PASSWORD   An app-specific password, not the primary one.
#
# AGENT_TZ              Required, an IANA zone name. The host may well run UTC while the owner
#                       does not, and Apple's web pickers store what they are typed as the page's
#                       zone, so the tools convert before typing. There is deliberately no
#                       default: a guessed zone moves a reminder by hours and nothing errors.
# AGENT_TZ_FILE         Optional. A file holding the zone, which wins over AGENT_TZ when it holds
#                       anything, because it is the thing that changes when the owner travels and
#                       a restart is not the moment to find that out. Defaults to
#                       /etc/agent/timezone. Whatever writes it needs no access to this account.
# AGENT_DEFAULT_LIST    Which reminder list a reminder goes to when the caller names none.
# AGENT_DEFAULT_CALENDAR
#                       Which calendar an event goes to when the caller names none. Set it: the
#                       fallback is whichever calendar sorts first, and on a real account that is
#                       often a shared one, so an event meant to be private is quietly not.
#
# ICLOUD_STATE          Everything this account writes for itself: the browser profile, the cookie
#                       jar, the per-app locks, the tab stamps. Defaults to `$HOME`.
# ICLOUD_SHARED_STATE   State two uids share: the blocked latch, the ask log, and the queue of
#                       writes deferred while Apple's grant had lapsed. A watchdog running as
#                       somebody else reads these, so it is deliberately outside this account's
#                       home. Defaults to `$HOME/shared-state`, which works for a single-uid
#                       install and is wrong for this one.
# ICLOUD_CDP            Where the resident Chromium listens for DevTools. Defaults to
#                       http://127.0.0.1:9222.
#
# MAIL_ATTACHMENTS_DIR  Where `read_mail(save_attachments=True)` writes. Shared: this server
#                       writes it and whichever uid stages a saved file reads it, so it is
#                       group-readable and never group-writable. Defaults to
#                       `$HOME/mail-attachments`.
#
# DRIVE_STAGING         Where the Drive pull leaves fetched files for another account to import.
#                       Defaults to `$ICLOUD_STATE/drive-staging`.
# DRIVE_ETAGS           The file recording what has already been fetched, so an unchanged file is
#                       skipped. Defaults to `$ICLOUD_STATE/state/drive-etags.json`.
# DRIVE_LIBRARIES       Which iCloud Drive app folders to pull, as a JSON array. These are folders
#                       an app writes into, so they are this deployment's facts and not this
#                       server's. `folder` copies every file below a folder, preserving its
#                       layout under `dest`; `tree` and `snapshot` support the two common export
#                       shapes documented in icloud_lib/drive_libraries.py. Empty means nothing is
#                       pulled, and the fetcher says so rather than guessing at folder names.
ICLOUD_APPLE_ID=you@icloud.com
ICLOUD_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
AGENT_TZ=Europe/Amsterdam
AGENT_TZ_FILE=/etc/agent/timezone
AGENT_DEFAULT_LIST=Reminders
AGENT_DEFAULT_CALENDAR=Personal
ICLOUD_STATE=/opt/agent-icloud
ICLOUD_SHARED_STATE=/var/lib/icloud-state
MAIL_ATTACHMENTS_DIR=/srv/mail-attachments
DRIVE_STAGING=/opt/agent-icloud/drive-staging
DRIVE_ETAGS=/opt/agent-icloud/state/drive-etags.json
DRIVE_LIBRARIES='[{"name": "Example App Exports", "kind": "folder", "dest": "example-app"}]'
